  "notes": "Owner's six-count weave, revised after visual review: keep the opening follow turn, then keep the lead on the left facing 270 and travelling backward on 3-5 while the follow faces 90 and travels forward. The follow cuts across the front on 6 as the couple opens to feet-apart promenade; the lead turns only 45 degrees here. Count 2 lands 15 cm less far along -x than the first proposal, giving room for genuine forward/backward progress. The separate three-count Promenade Walk and Close completes the owner's nine-count combination. Entry and exit exactly match the existing promenade-apart stance; no Whisk setup is required. The first step, support alternation, 1-2-3 / 1-2-3 timing and rise are preserved. Dimensions, underturned alignment and curved routes are provisional for subjective review, not an exact syllabus chart. Standard six-count context: https://www.ballroomdancers.com/dances/info.asp?sid=495 and https://ballroomguide.github.io/BallroomGuide/standard/waltz/weave_from_pp.html . All authoring and body checks run without exclusions; dense tests cover complete footprints and thigh/shin capsules with linear and eased playback."
